<o:EntityAttribute Id="o720">
<a:ObjectID>0AE71A0D-8051-4CB6-8582-06F89C528BB5</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Company_Code</a:Name>
<a:Code>T047M_BUKRS</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1718371148</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1724650482</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The company code is the central organizational unit of external accounting within the SAP System. You must define at least one company code before implementing the Financial Accounting component. The business transactions relevant for Financial Accounting are entered, saved, and evaluated at company code level.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A4</a:DataType>
<a:Length>4</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,126={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,5=BUKRS
