{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o766">
<a:ObjectID>94F44BD9-8AF7-49A5-A35B-F12EF16A6EE6</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Sales_Price_Calculation_Relevant_To_Pricing</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_VKKAL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The indicator can be maintained during definition of condition types and is taken as a default value when condition records are generated. This default can be changed when the &quot;Pricing relevance can be changed&quot; indicator is set.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A1</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,126={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,5=VKKAL
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o767">
<a:ObjectID>68E80E1D-1E54-4F1E-99F6-881963D4F5EF</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Sp_Calculation_Relevant_Pricing</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_VKOBL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>If this indicator is set, you can define for each condition record individually whether it is to be taken into account in the sales price calculation function</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A1</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,126={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,5=VKOBL
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o768">
<a:ObjectID>D250C992-6182-436E-8D9F-79729B221A7E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Reference_Application</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_RKAPPL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>we have to create condition records once for condition types that are very similar. You can also refer to condition records from other applications.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A2</a:DataType>
<a:Length>2</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,127={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,6=RKAPPL
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o769">
<a:ObjectID>07E4DCD6-5687-4B02-AE64-21E0903EC1DC</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Reference_Condition_Type</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_RKSCHL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>If we need to use different condition types for the same condition. These can differ in the access sequence, the description, the reference step of the pricing procedure or the calculation type, for example.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A4</a:DataType>
<a:Length>4</a:Length>
<a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>1</a:LogicalAttribute.Mandatory>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,127={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,6=RKSCHL
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o770">
<a:ObjectID>27C11F2B-F179-4816-BA41-0F0E57E427E2</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Calculation_Base</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_BERGL</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>During shipment costing, the system determines the shipment cost sub-items from the different calculation bases of the condition types of a pricing procedure. Actual calculation of the shipment costs is then carried out in each sub-item.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A1</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,126={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,5=BERGL
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o771">
<a:ObjectID>44AD9793-53AE-4DF8-B5AF-05D6D62A1507</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Packaging_Material_Type</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_VHART</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The packaging material type that you enter here is linked to a material group for packaging materials, which you assign to a material in the material master. As you assemble the handling unit, you call up a list of packaging materials that are allowed for an item that you want to pack. This system puts together this list by matching the material group for packaging materials for that item with the appropriate packaging material types</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A4</a:DataType>
<a:Length>4</a:Length>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,126={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,5=VHART
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o772">
<a:ObjectID>D0D99D7E-BF56-4C69-866A-B8D284E7838E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Rounding_Difference_Comparison</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_RDIFA</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Indicator that controls whether rounding difference is settled for group conditions with a group key routine. If the indicator is set, the system compares the condition value at header level with the total of the condition values at item level. The difference is then added to the largest item.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A1</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,126={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,5=RDIFA
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o773">
<a:ObjectID>7766EFF2-5A2D-4415-BFF3-5B4146411184</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Condition_Intercompany_Billing</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_KFKIV</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Intercompany conditions are usually statistical in the sales order and the customer invoice and not statistical in the intercompany invoice.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A1</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,126={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,5=KFKIV
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
