</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o791">
<a:ObjectID>3C32BB1C-B169-4FE1-ADB2-E9FCB6524877</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Process_Conditions_Value_Equals_Zero</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_VAL_ZERO</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Using this indicator, you can control how conditions with value equal to zero are processed.
If you leave this field blank, the following applies:
Conditions are not considered in the condition exclusion logic when their value is equal to zero.
Price conditions are deactivated during the price calculation if their amount and value are equal to zero.
If you set the value of this indicator to &quot;A&quot; for this condition type, the following applies:
Conditions of this type will be considered in the exclusion logic even if their value is equal to zero.
If this is a condition type with condition class &quot;Price&quot;, conditions of this type will not be deactivated during the price calculation.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A1</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,129={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,8=VAL_ZERO
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o792">
<a:ObjectID>506E7403-2247-4A81-B6B4-603237637635</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Condition_Enabled_Commodity_Pricing_Engine</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_IS_CPE_ENABLED</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>If this indicator is set, you can assign a CPE formula to a condition type, either by using the formula assembly, or directly in a logistics document.
While the commodity pricing is performed, the condition is calculated using the assigned CPE formula.
If you set this indicator, each condition with calculation type &#39;Q&#39; (Commodity Pricing) is calculated by the formula assembly average pricing</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A1</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,136={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,14=IS_CPE_ENABLED
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
<c:RelatedCodeTerms>
<o:Shortcut Ref="o550"/>
<o:Shortcut Ref="o788"/>
</c:RelatedCodeTerms>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o793">
<a:ObjectID>A1714E81-A971-4AC2-B466-50AC5962B04D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Gross_Net_Pricing_Indicator</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_OIGRNET</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Defines whether the value of a condition type is always to be calculated using a gross or a net volume, or whether the gross/net rule on the line item (OIGNRULE) is to be examined. If the value is blank, normal processing takes place, that is, the volume used follows the volume that is used to define the condition record.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>A1</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{930ED224-E528-44BB-9634-E758B0B77368},Shell_Attribute_Properties,128={F1CC8296-4560-4EC5-9345-1B45E56FBDE2},SAP_Field_Name,7=OIGRNET
{47E6A3AE-AA47-425C-AA05-CF089FE2BD43},SAP_Table_Name,5=T685A

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
</o:EntityAttribute>
<o:EntityAttribute Id="o794">
<a:ObjectID>926B6AC3-69FE-432B-A920-27B0478C0950</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Invoice_Cycle</a:Name>
<a:Code>T685A_OIINVCYC</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719815732</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1719815732</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Key identifying an invoicing cycle</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>N1</a:DataType>
<a:Length>1</a:Length>
