<o:Entity Id="o262">
<a:ObjectID>0B03534C-058B-439C-B5D0-F5C6DC05C0EA</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>DUNNING_AREA_FOR_CUSTOMER_MASTER</a:Name>
<a:Code>KNB5</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1719579393</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Biren.Shah2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1723456440</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Dunning is the process of methodically communicating with customers to ensure the collection of accounts receivable.
The SAP system allows you to dun business partners automatically. The system duns the open items from business partner accounts in which the overdue items create a debit balance. The dunning program selects the overdue open items, determines the dunning level of the account in question, and creates a dunning notice.

You can use the dunning program to dun both customers and vendors. It may be necessary to dun a vendor if he or she has a debit balance as a result of a credit memo. If a customer is also a vendor, you can offset the account balances against one another.

SAP table: KNB5
</a:Comment>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{77894B2F-5C8A-41A3-AAF2-C1D07AC2DAD1},BIM-core,651={8DB6F0D8-502C-4315-805C-4AC30C42CB29},CommerciallySensitiveInformation,34=Commercially Sensitive Information
