<a:Comment>This entity is in alignment with the EFDM model.</a:Comment>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{F14358E6-B1E1-4852-B322-164BF9629076},EFDM_Entity_Attributes,3812={34E60362-1B40-42AC-87BD-34316D85531D},SAP_Standard_Definition,193=The banks that Shell has an account with. They are used to process payment transactions. Each house bank account is linked to a bank account in bank account master data via a connectivity path.
{66AB24CA-DDD5-4173-96CD-AC09512972BE},Shell_Usage_Guide,583=House banks are used to define where a supplier should be paid from. It can be hard coded on a vendor, directly on the invoice, or derived by default via payment program (best practice is to have one bank account per currency for payments and use the payment program to automatically derive the house banks based on payment method and currency).  In a JVA dedicated banking environment the house bank can be derived from the funding group. The house bank is used for automatic payments and bank reconciliation interfaces
The list of House Banks maintained by Cash Management is here
