<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{F14358E6-B1E1-4852-B322-164BF9629076},EFDM_Entity_Attributes,3408={34E60362-1B40-42AC-87BD-34316D85531D},SAP_Standard_Definition,48=Key used to define exchange rates in the system.
{66AB24CA-DDD5-4173-96CD-AC09512972BE},Shell_Usage_Guide,658=Different exchange rates can be defined for each currency pair and these exchange rates are differentiated using the exchange rate type.  Different exchange rates can be for the following purposes, for example: valuation, conversion, translation, planning.
For posting and clearing, the system uses the exchange rate type M (average rate). This exchange rate type must be entered in the system and the exchange rates for this type must be also entered.
The following exchange rate types exist:
·         Buying rate
·         Bank selling rate
·         Average rate
·         Historical exchange rate
The standard S4HANA exchange rate types are here.
