<o:Entity Id="o242">
<a:ObjectID>5976657B-6A83-4168-BAE4-48C80DE0F5AC</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>CUSTOMER_PAYMENT_TERMS</a:Name>
<a:Code>TVZB</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1690465007</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Sridhar.Yilapavanam2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1723456353</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Terms of payment are used in SAP to determine the due date and discount calculation for accounts receivable (A/R) and accounts payable (A/P) postings . Terms of payment are maintained in vendor and customer master records or contracts to support default values  being updated during sales/purchase order creation and transaction processing.  These defaulted values shouldn’t  be changed by the users.
You can include terms of payment as part of your promotional strategy. For example, when you create master data for promotions or sales deals, you can specify special values for the following payment-related data:
Terms of Payment
Fixed value date
Additional value days
If you create a sales deal as part of a promotion in which you have already specified special terms of payment, these values are automatically copied into the sales deal. When you create condition records as part of a sales deal in which you have specified special payment terms, the system automatically copies the terms into the condition record.

SAP table: TVZB</a:Comment>
