<o:Entity Id="o237">
<a:ObjectID>2B7C10CF-B19D-455A-B3A4-88EFED0CC978</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>SALES_AREA</a:Name>
<a:Code>TVTA</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1690358184</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Sridhar.Yilapavanam2</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1724650482</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Biren.Shah2</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A Sales Area is a specific combination of Sales Organization + Distribution Channel + Division. A defined Sales Area is required to complete any sales activities.
Shell use sales areas to define the Legal entity providing a service alongside the function/business in that entity and the service type of the function. The Sales area therefore makes up a combination of the selling entity, the function/business and service type (sales org, distribution channel and division).  Customers (OU&#39;s) are then extended to the Sales Area and should closely map to the types of services customers can expect to receive from the Service providers or functions.
Might be subject to change due to some changes in the future process design.

SAP table: TVTA</a:Comment>
